page('privacy.html','Privacy and cookies','<p>This page explains what we collect when you use the UK Short-Let Rules Tracker. We keep it short.</p><h2>Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h2><p>If you click <b>Accept</b> on the cookie bar, we use Google Analytics 4 to count page views and which tools are used (for example the checker, levy calculator and signup forms). This sets analytics cookies. We do not use advertising cookies, and ad features stay switched off. If you click <b>Reject</b>, or make no choice, no analytics cookies are set. You can change your mind any time with the <a href="#" class="ck-open">Cookie settings</a> link at the bottom of every page. Your choice is stored in your browser (local storage).</p><h2>Cloudflare Web Analytics</h2><p>We may also use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless: it counts visits without cookies or tracking you across sites.</p><h2>Newsletter and alerts</h2><p>If you sign up for the newsletter or council alerts, we store your email address (and the council you chose, for alerts) with our email provider, Resend, only to send those emails. Every email has an unsubscribe link. We never sell or share your address.</p><h2>Feedback</h2><p>Feedback you send through the "Did this answer your question?" box comes to us by email with the page address. Your email address is optional.</p><h2>Embedded widgets</h2><p>The embeddable checker and levy calculator do not load analytics or set cookies.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>Questions or requests about your data: <a href="mailto:hello@ukshortletrules.co.uk">hello@ukshortletrules.co.uk</a>.</p><p>The UK Short-Let Rules team</p>',desc='What the UK Short-Let Rules Tracker collects: optional Google Analytics 4 with consent, cookieless Cloudflare Web Analytics, and newsletter emails via Resend.')
page('sponsor.html','Sponsor the tracker','<p>The UK Short-Let Rules Tracker is a free, independent guide to the rules for UK holiday-let and short-term-let hosts.</p><p>If you would like to sponsor the tracker, or talk about another way of working together, please get in touch: <a href="mailto:hello@ukshortletrules.co.uk">hello@ukshortletrules.co.uk</a>.</p><p>Any sponsorship would be clearly labelled, and sponsors never affect the content.</p>')

